Almost every screen in EduConnect depends on something configured on another screen. Doing this in
order takes an afternoon; doing it out of order means redoing parts of it.

Each step links to its own tutorial.

## 1. The calendar

**Administration → Settings**, then **Administration → Holidays**.

Working days, term dates, holidays and term breaks. Everything attendance-related is a percentage of
these, so getting them in first means your figures are right from day one instead of being corrected
in week three.

→ [Set Holidays, Terms and Working Days](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-holidays-and-terms)

## 2. People and places

1. **Classes** — → [Add a Class](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-class)
2. **Teachers**, with the subjects each one teaches — →
   [Add a Teacher](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-teacher)
3. **Students**, into their classes — →
   [Add a Student](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student) or
   [Import from Excel](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-import-students)
4. Set the **class teacher** on each class.

Teachers before students, because a class with a teacher on it is one less thing to revisit.

## 3. Logins

**Administration → Users**, then **Administration → Access Control**.

A teacher record is not a login. Create the accounts, then decide what each role can open.

→ [Add a User and Grant Access](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-users-and-access)

## 4. The timetable chain

Strictly in this order — each step is the input to the next:

1. **Bell Schedule** — → [Set Up the Bell Schedule](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-bell-schedule)
2. **Subjects & Rules**, **Subject Groups**, **Classrooms**, **Teacher Constraints** — the rest of
   **Timetable → Configuration**
3. **Grade Curriculum**, then **Apply to Grade** — →
   [Create or Edit a Grade Curriculum](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-grade-curriculum)
4. **Class Subjects**, assigning a teacher to each — →
   [Assign Subjects and Teachers](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-class-subjects)
5. **Generate** — → [Generate the Timetable](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-generate-timetable)

Generating with an incomplete chain is the single most common source of "the timetable doesn't
work". The generator can only place what steps 1–4 have told it about.

## 5. Money

1. **Fee Setup** — the fee types and their instalments →
   [Set Up Fees](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-fee-setup)
2. **Discounts** — scholarships, sibling and staff reductions →
   [Set Up and Grant Discounts](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-discounts)
3. **Portal Access Rules** — what unpaid fees do to a parent's portal access
4. Online payments, in **Administration → Settings**, if you take card payments

Fees before students start paying, obviously — but also before the term starts, since due dates are
what make a charge overdue.

## 6. Cards

Add blank cards to the pool, upload the card design, and make sure every student and teacher record
has an **RFID**. A record without one can never register attendance.

→ [Issue and Replace ID Cards](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-id-cards)

## 7. What parents see

1. **Handbook** — → [Write and Publish the Student Handbook](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-handbook)
2. **Prospectus**, if you take admissions through the portal
3. Institute branding and terminology in **Administration → Settings** —
   [why the wording changes](/docs/shared-institute-branding)

## 8. Then, in term

- Attendance daily — [as a teacher](/docs/educonnect-teacher-taking-attendance)
- [Exams](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-create-an-exam) and
  [results](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-enter-exam-results) as they happen
- [Day close](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-day-close) each evening
- [Progress reports](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-progress-reports) at the end of term
